Patch 14: promote the speed-4 warp search pattern to speed 3.

Standalone. Composes with patches 13, 15 and 16.

Of the three features that genuinely clear their bar at speed 4 in the
101-feature study, two have now been promoted to speed 3 and both returned at
or above their speed-4 measurement:

    prune_tx_type_using_stats   +4.90% @ s4  ->  +6.12% @ s3   (ratio 34.0)
    dc_blk_pred_level           +3.08% @ s4  ->  +3.08% @ s3   (ratio ~308)
    warp_search_method          +1.65% @ s4  ->  not promoted

This patch promotes the third. WARP_SEARCH_DIAMOND replaces the square warp
search pattern with a diamond one; speed 3 currently pays for the wider pattern.

The direction is principled rather than hopeful: a pattern-reduction feature
saves more where the search it replaces is deeper, and speed 3 searches warp
parameters harder than speed 4 does. The same scaling appeared in the combined
runs on this branch, where an identical patch set gained +30.7% at speed 2
against +20.3% at speed 4 for essentially unchanged BD-rate.

The risk is that this is the thinnest of the three margins: ratio 20.6 measured
against a speed-3 bar of 25. If time saving and BD-rate scale together on
promotion -- as they roughly did for transform-statistics pruning, whose ratio
fell from 49.0 to 34.0 when it moved from speed 4 to speed 3 -- then the ratio
barely moves and this fails. It clears only if the extra warp search at speed 3
turns out to be disproportionately redundant.

Because of that, this is deliberately a separate arm from patch 13 rather than
bundled with it. Bundling a likely pass with a marginal one costs the ability to
tell which did what, and this branch has already paid for that lesson once.

Expected: +1.5% to +2.5% speedup at speed 3 with BD-rate near +0.08%. Whether
the resulting ratio clears 25 is the open question and the reason to run it.

diff --git a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
index f363519..fdfbfd9 100644
--- a/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
+++ b/av2/encoder/speed_features.c
