+    // 20 -- a genuine pass, and the only one of the three genuine speed-4
+    // passes not yet promoted. The other two, transform-statistics pruning and
+    // DC-block prediction, were promoted to speed 3 and returned +6.12% and
+    // +3.08%, both at or above their speed-4 measurements.
+    //
+    // That direction is expected rather than lucky: a pattern-reduction feature
+    // saves more where the search it replaces is deeper, and speed 3 searches
+    // warp parameters harder than speed 4. The same scaling appeared in the
+    // combined runs on this branch, where an identical patch set gained +30.7%
+    // at speed 2 against +20.3% at speed 4 for near-identical BD-rate.
+    //
+    // This is the thinnest of the three margins: 20.6 measured against a
+    // speed-3 bar of 25. If time and BD-rate scale together on promotion -- as
+    // they roughly did for tx-stat pruning, whose ratio fell 49.0 -> 34.0 -- the
